{"source_slots":{"s4":"I'll try the 1:1.5 ratio and keep an eye on it. I'm making a coconut curry, so the liquid is pretty rich. I guess I'll see how it goes.","s5":"That sounds delicious! A coconut curry is going to be wonderful, and using that 1:1.5 ratio should give you a good balance—it should stay moist without becoming too mushy. 

Let me know how the texture looks after a few minutes; if it feels like it's getting too soft, you can always add a little more liquid at the end to adjust the consistency.

Enjoy the process—I'm sure your curry will turn out perfectly!"}}
